---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';
import AccountWorkspace from '../../components/AccountWorkspace';
import { PRO_FAQ, PRO_PRICES, proSchema } from '../../lib/pro-page.mjs';
import '../../styles/account.css';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Pro' }];
const schema = proSchema('https://deadhangs.com/pro/');
---
<Article title="DeadHangs Pro: Cloud Sync and Progress History" description="DeadHangs Pro keeps your dead hang log in your account so you can open it on another device, with progress history by date. £4.99 a month or £39 a year. The timer and log stay free." crumbs={crumbs} schema={schema} wide>
  <section class="pro-hero" aria-labelledby="pro-title">
    <div class="pro-hero-copy">
      <nav class="article-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Pro</span></li></ol></nav>
      <h1 id="pro-title" class="pro-h1">Your dead hang log, on every device.</h1>
      <p class="pro-price"><span class="pro-price-figure">£{PRO_PRICES.monthly}</span> a month <span class="pro-price-or">or</span> <span class="pro-price-figure">£{PRO_PRICES.yearly}</span> a year</p>
      <p class="pro-price-note">Yearly is about 35% less than twelve monthly payments (£59.88). Cancel renewal any time; Pro normally runs to the end of the paid period.</p>
      <ul class="pro-gets" aria-label="What Pro adds">
        <li>Merge the holds from the free timer into your account.</li>
        <li>Copy them to any other phone or computer.</li>
        <li>Progress history by date, up to 200 cloud entries.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="pro-hero-action">
      <AccountWorkspace pricing client:load />
      <noscript><p class="pro-noscript">Enable JavaScript to sign in and choose a plan.</p></noscript>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pro-body">
    <section class="pro-split" aria-labelledby="pro-why-title">
      <figure class="pro-example">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 480 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="pro-example-title pro-example-desc" class="pro-example-svg">
          <title id="pro-example-title">Example of Pro progress history</title>
          <desc id="pro-example-desc">An example, not real data: one setup, unassisted on a pull-up bar, with best recorded hold 62 seconds, latest daily best 58 seconds and a change of plus 21 seconds from the first day, above a table of four dated entries.</desc>
          <rect x="0.5" y="0.5" width="479" height="329" class="pe-frame" />
          <rect x="356" y="14" width="110" height="26" class="pe-tag" />
          <text x="411" y="32" text-anchor="middle" class="pe-tag-text">EXAMPLE</text>
          <text x="20" y="34" class="pe-h">Progress from your cloud entries</text>
          <text x="20" y="62" class="pe-sub">Unassisted · Pull-up bar · Overhand grip</text>
          <line x1="20" y1="78" x2="460" y2="78" class="pe-rule" />
          <text x="20" y="102" class="pe-label">Best recorded</text>
          <text x="20" y="132" class="pe-num">62 s</text>
          <text x="170" y="102" class="pe-label">Latest daily best</text>
          <text x="170" y="132" class="pe-num">58 s</text>
          <text x="320" y="102" class="pe-label">Change from first day</text>
          <text x="320" y="132" class="pe-num pe-up">+21 s</text>
          <rect x="20" y="156" width="440" height="30" class="pe-th" />
          <text x="32" y="176" class="pe-cell pe-bold">Date</text><text x="170" y="176" class="pe-cell pe-bold">Hold</text><text x="250" y="176" class="pe-cell pe-bold">Sets</text><text x="320" y="176" class="pe-cell pe-bold">Setup</text>
          <g class="pe-cell">
            <text x="32" y="210">9 Nov 2026</text><text x="170" y="210">58 s</text><text x="250" y="210">3</text><text x="320" y="210">Unassisted</text>
            <text x="32" y="240">6 Nov 2026</text><text x="170" y="240">62 s</text><text x="250" y="240">3</text><text x="320" y="240">Max test</text>
            <text x="32" y="270">3 Nov 2026</text><text x="170" y="270">52 s</text><text x="250" y="270">3</text><text x="320" y="270">Unassisted</text>
            <text x="32" y="300">30 Oct 2026</text><text x="170" y="300">44 s</text><text x="250" y="300">4</text><text x="320" y="300">Unassisted</text>
          </g>
          <line x1="20" y1="218" x2="460" y2="218" class="pe-rule" /><line x1="20" y1="248" x2="460" y2="248" class="pe-rule" /><line x1="20" y1="278" x2="460" y2="278" class="pe-rule" />
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Example with made-up values, not a real account. It shows the shape of the history on the account page: daily bests within one setup and every cloud entry by date.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="pro-why">
        <h2 id="pro-why-title">Why the free log is not enough on its own</h2>
        <p>The free timer saves your holds in this browser. That keeps them private. The log also has limits you only notice when it is too late:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Clearing browsing data deletes it. Some browsers also remove storage for sites you have not visited for a while.</li>
          <li>A new phone starts with an empty log.</li>
          <li>Your phone and your laptop each keep a separate log.</li>
          <li>Export and import work on every plan. You have to remember to do them by hand.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Pro keeps a copy in your account. You choose when to merge. Nothing is sent until you do.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pro-section" aria-labelledby="pro-compare-title">
      <h2 id="pro-compare-title">Free and Pro compared</h2>
      <div class="pro-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Comparison table, scrolls sideways on small screens">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Free</th><th scope="col">Pro</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Interval timer, all four modes</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Training log in this browser, up to 200 entries</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Progress on this device, calculators and plans</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">CSV export, backup and import on the device</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Google sign-in</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Account export and deletion</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Merge your device log into your account, up to 200 cloud entries</th><td>Not included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Copy your cloud log to another device</th><td>Not included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Progress history from your cloud entries, by date</th><td>Not included</td><td>Included</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Price</th><td>£0</td><td>£4.99 a month or £39 a year</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pro-section" aria-labelledby="pro-how-title">
      <h2 id="pro-how-title">How it works</h2>
      <ol class="pro-steps">
        <li><strong>Sign in and choose a plan.</strong> Use your Google account on this page and pick monthly or yearly. Signing in uploads nothing.</li>
        <li><strong>Train with the free timer.</strong> Record your holds in the <a href="/training-log/">timer and log</a> as you do now. They save on the device first.</li>
        <li><strong>Merge and then copy down.</strong> On your account page merge the device entries into your cloud log. On your other device sign in with the same Google account and copy the cloud entries to that device. Sync is manual. You always choose what moves.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="pro-section" aria-labelledby="pro-faq-title">
      <h2 id="pro-faq-title">Questions before you pay</h2>
      <div class="pro-faq">
        {PRO_FAQ.map((item) => (
          <div class="pro-faq-item">
            <h3>{item.q}</h3>
            <p set:html={item.html} />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="pro-launch">DeadHangs Pro launched in November 2026. Read the full <a href="/terms/">terms</a> and <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Article>
